  "findings": [
    "Deep native DCN has two m=1 diodes with distinct cathode nets; parent call connects both to vss. Deep native DCP likewise has distinct anodes connected by the parent. Reference children already combine each pair into m=2; deep children fail 3 layout vs 2 reference devices and parent comparison is skipped.",
    "Flat extraction merges both diode pairs into m=2, but remains 5 layout vs 6 reference devices. Native flat output retains distinct anode|iovss and guard|iovss conductors; names do not prove a physical join.",
    "Flat native layout has one substrate node; captured reference H section has SUB!, I1.SUB!, I2.SUB!. Pinned vendor CDL declares no .GLOBAL; globally joining these names would change the reference contract.",
    "Substantial independent strict tap A/P differences remain, including VSS 24/160.6 against 23.523/19.4. Under fixed tap-recognition masks and parameters, external metal-only connections cannot remove that independent mismatch. Actual parent extraction could change overlapping recognition geometry; that has not been measured.",
    "Native CustomTap preserves ordered TIE/WELL and enabled A/P comparison. No A/P waiver, geometry edit, model substitution or arbitrary name/global union is justified by these observations."
  ],
